WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.900
Carbon is carbon.

2
00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:05.100
Yet not every carbon
atom has the same mass.

3
00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:09.330
There is carbon-12,
carbon-13 and carbon-14:

4
00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:12.920
three kinds of carbon,
each with its own mass.

5
00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:15.600
And one of them behaves very differently.

6
00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:18.300
Carbon-14 is radioactive.

7
00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:20.570
Carbon-12 is not.

8
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.680
If they are all carbon,
with the same chemistry,

9
00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:25.780
what is different inside them?

10
00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.660
In this mission, you'll
zoom into the atom,

11
00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:34.230
down to a nucleus up to 100 000
times smaller than the atom itself.

12
00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:38.380
Then you'll learn to read the short
code written for every nucleus:

13
00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:40.630
one symbol, two numbers.

14
00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:45.170
Your mission: find out what makes
one carbon atom heavier than another.
